\documentclass{article}
\title{Multiaxial Fatigue of Additively Manufactured Titanium Alloys}
\author{L. Brandt and O. Mensah}
\date{May 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\input{chapters/intro}
\input{chapters/methods}
\input{chapters/results}
\end{document}

\section{Results}
Life under proportional loading exceeds life under non-proportional loading.
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
\hline
Condition & Cycles to initiation \\
\hline
Machined surface & 38800 \\
As-built & 412 & 358 \\
Polished & 44100 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
The as-built condition fails earliest in every loading path we tested.

